# Rank 1394 / CVE-2026-10611 (GHSA-679g-pp8v-jvg4, CWE-287):
# MISP is a CakePHP 2 application. Its AppController::beforeFilter() calls
# _loadAuthenticationPlugins() on every request, which installs whatever
# authentication plugins `Security.auth` names (LDAP being the deployed case) and
# then, at app/Controller/AppController.php:1403-1411, promotes the request to a
# fully authenticated session the moment a plugin returns a user record:
#
#   if ($this->Auth->startup($this)) {
#       $user = $this->Auth->user();
#       if ($user) {
#           $this->User->updateLoginTimes($user);
#           // User found in the db, add the user info to the session
#           $this->Session->renew();
#           $this->Session->write(AuthComponent::$sessionKey, $user);
#       }
#   }
#
# The weakness, stated from the diff rather than from the advisory: the second
# factor is enforced in one place only -- UsersController::login(), which on
# `Security.otp_disabled == false && $user['totp']` writes the identity to a
# *pending* session slot (`otp_user`) and redirects to /users/otp instead of
# writing AuthComponent::$sessionKey. The plugin path above skips that step
# entirely. It writes the real auth session key directly, from beforeFilter,
# before UsersController::login() ever runs. With `LdapAuth.mixedAuth=true` and
# `Security.require_otp=true` the first factor alone therefore produces a session
# that every subsequent request accepts: the browser sits on the OTP form, but any
# other URL is authenticated. The authentication decision is completed on
# one factor, in a request-lifecycle hook, using the framework's internal session
# slot rather than its login API -- so nothing that the login action enforces
# after the password check applies.
#
# 39b3cb15aac4318afdd2ab63b96c2eac12b271fe adds 54 lines to that one file: a new
# private __pluginLoginRequiresOtp($user) that re-implements the login action's OTP
# branch (TOTP/HOTP under `Security.otp_disabled` and `class_exists('\OTPHP\TOTP')`,
# e-mail OTP under `Security.email_otp_enabled`), writes the pending slot,
# redirects unless the current action is `otp`/`email_otp`, and returns
# true; and, in _loadAuthenticationPlugins, a three-line guard that returns before
# the session is established:
#
#   +   if ($this->__pluginLoginRequiresOtp($user)) {
#   +       return;
#   +   }
#
# The row is correct as written: repository and commit both check out, and
# both hold: MISP/MISP resolves, 39b3cb15aa is a single-file security fix by a MISP
# core maintainer whose subject names this exact bypass, and the vulnerable
# construct is present at 39b3cb15aa^ -- _loadAuthenticationPlugins contains no
# OTP, TOTP or second-factor reference of any kind. The recorded CWE-287 is
# defensible; CWE-288 (bypass using an alternate path) is the tighter fit, since
# the control exists and this path goes around it. No corpus correction.
#
# MISP does not finish inside the loop's bound: `timeout 180 ./bin/vyql scan
# --cache off --max-ram 6GB` over the whole checkout (2608 files, 522 .php and
# 1145 .ctp) is killed at 180s. Measurements below are therefore a bounded subtree
# scan of app/Controller (91 PHP files, 10.7s) plus an exhaustive grep enumeration
# of the shape's reachable set. The enumeration is decisive and small:
# `AuthComponent::$sessionKey` appears six times in the entire repository, all but
# one in app/Controller/AppController.php -- three writes (:564 in
# __loginByAuthKey, :1323 in __customAuthentication, :1409 in
# _loadAuthenticationPlugins), one read at :271, one reset at :1743, and one
# doc-comment mention in app/Controller/Component/ApacheSecureAuthComponent.php.
# `Auth->startup(` occurs exactly once, at :1403. So the whole reachable set of
# "hand-written CakePHP auth session" in MISP is three sites in one file, all
# inside the bounded subtree, and the fixing commit touches one of the three.
#
# What fires today: app/Controller at 39b3cb15aa^ and at 39b3cb15aa each report
# **356 findings, three runs apiece, and `vyql diff` of the two JSON reports says
# `identical -- finding-set preserved` (0 added, 0 removed)**. Nothing lands in
# _loadAuthenticationPlugins in either revision; AppController.php's own rows are
# VYQL-CRY-003 at :465 and VYQL-INJ-004 / VYQL-RF-003 clusters at :1075, :1615 and
# :1759. `vyql match` over the vulnerable file labels the whole method not at all
# except for one incidental `code.HtmlRender` -- `unset($this->Auth->authenticate
# ['Form'])` lowers as `path=echo`, which is a separate cosmetic defect worth
# knowing about. `-flags only` yields three flags for the file, none of them here.
#
# ATTENTION. The construct is bindable; the revisions are not discriminable. Both halves
# are measured with throwaway PHP presence bindings emitting the existing
# code.AuthFlowBypassReview (CWE-287, `expected: [core.AuthenticationCheck]`),
# scored with `-flags only` against both revisions.
#
# 1. The construct alone, function scope:
#      node.scope == "function" and node.context.language == "php"
#      and node.context.callPath contains "$this.Session.write"
#      and node.context.callArg contains "$this.Session.write:AuthComponent::$sessionKey"
#    fires on both revisions, as it must -- the patched method still writes the key.
#    On the app/Controller subtree it is 5 flags at 39b3cb15aa^ and 6 at
#    39b3cb15aa, and only three of those are write sites: :497 __loginByAuthKey,
#    :1286 __customAuthentication, :1388 _loadAuthenticationPlugins, plus :110
#    beforeFilter and :597 __verifyUser, which contain no such write at all, plus
#    :1431 __pluginLoginRequiresOtp on the fixed revision. That over-attribution is
#    the routing leak recorded in this campaign's PHP notes, measured again here:
#    `call_arg:` and `call_path:` are both in flagASTRoutingValuePrefixes
#    (internal/bindings/bindings_match.go:730), so the clause matches through the
#    file-wide AST path rather than the node's own str_args. There is no confined
#    substitute for this particular fact: `call_arg_method:write:AuthComponent::
#    $sessionKey` is emitted by the frontend (php.go:610) and would be confined,
#    but no presence-context field maps to that prefix -- v2PresenceValuePrefix
#    (internal/bindings/compile_presence.go:380) exposes assignCallMethod and not
#    callArgMethod.
#
# 2. The same clause with the second factor negated over the node's own text:
#      and not containsAny(node.token, ["otp", "OTP", "Otp", "mfa", "Mfa",
#                                       "twoFactor", "two_factor"])
#    does discriminate the minimal pair -- 1 flag on the vulnerable method, 0 on
#    the patched one -- and on the real files it is 3 flags at 39b3cb15aa^ and 2 at
#    39b3cb15aa. It is still not shippable, for two independent reasons, and the
#    third case below pins the first of them:
#
#    (a) **the only thing it discriminates on is the fixed revision's own method name.**
#        Renaming __pluginLoginRequiresOtp to __pluginLoginRequiresSecondFactor,
#        changing nothing else, restores the flag on the patched file (0 -> 1). The
#        negation is reading the substring "Otp" out of the identifier in
#        `if ($this->__pluginLoginRequiresOtp($user))`; the whole OTP vocabulary
#        the fixed revision actually adds -- Configure::read('Security.otp_disabled'),
#        $user['totp'], class_exists('\OTPHP\TOTP'), Session->write('otp_user'),
#        the redirect -- lives in the callee's body, which the calling function's
#        context facts do not include. That is the engine gap below, and keying on
#        the predicate's name instead is the "fixing commit's own layout"
#        discriminator this campaign has had rejected before.
#
#    (b) **even with that fact, the label is 1-in-3 on the vulnerable tree.** The
#        two survivors at 39b3cb15aa are __loginByAuthKey (:497, API key
#        authentication) and __customAuthentication (:1286, header
#        authentication). Both write AuthComponent::$sessionKey with no OTP
#        anywhere near them, both are still there at the fixed revision, and MISP left
#        them alone deliberately -- an OTP challenge is meaningless for a
#        non-interactive API key. Case 4 below is __loginByAuthKey, so this is
#        pinned rather than asserted.
#
# 3. Class scope, the only scope that holds both the write and the OTP vocabulary
#    on the patched revision, is dead in the other direction: the same negation
#    yields 0 flags on *both* revisions, because the vulnerable AppController
#    says `otp` at :409 (preAuthActions), :410
#    (Security.email_otp_enabled) and :735 (Security.otp_required). Co-membership
#    in an 1800-line controller proves nothing about the path, which is the
#    whole-file-text trap this campaign has had rejected twice.
#
# Engine gap, not mechanical: PHP is the third language in which "the fixed revision extracts
# the security check into a sibling method and calls it" is invisible to the
# calling function's context facts -- Rust at 1364 (where the delegated call also
# does not resolve), JavaScript/TypeScript at 1372 (where it does), and PHP here,
# where it is worse than either: phpFunctionContext walks only the declaring
# function's body, *and* `$this->__pluginLoginRequiresOtp(...)` does not resolve at
# all, for the reason localised at 1376 -- the frontend declares SelfName "this"
# while the receiver text is `$this`, so `sc.typ` has no self entry and resolution
# falls back to program-wide short-name matching. Closing it needs a design
# decision about attributing a callee's facts to its caller across every PHP scan,
# and per measurement 2(b) it is necessary but not sufficient for this rank.
#
# The four cases are the pinned miss and the pair that isolates its cause. Case 1
# is the real vulnerable method and case 2 the real patched one, both rejected
# today. Case 3 is case 2 with the helper renamed so that no "otp" substring
# survives in the guarded method: any binding that separated case 1 from case 2
# would report case 3, which is the same fix. Case 4 is the sibling API-key path
# from the same class, which carries the identical construct and is correct as
# written.
#
# verify_current_expected: attention-engine-gap, all four forms rejected.

test "rank1394: an authentication plugin's user record establishes the CakePHP auth session during beforeFilter with no second-factor challenge"
  lang php
  file app/Controller/AppController.php
  reject VYQL-AUTH-004
  reject_review code.AuthFlowBypassReview
  reject_review code.MissingSessionRotationAfterAuthentication
  code
  ```
  <?php
  App::uses('Controller', 'Controller');

  class AppController extends Controller
  {
      public function beforeFilter()
      {
          if (!$this->Session->read(AuthComponent::$sessionKey)) {
              $this->_loadAuthenticationPlugins();
          }
      }

      /**
       * @throws Exception
       */
      protected function _loadAuthenticationPlugins()
      {
          // load authentication plugins from Configure::read('Security.auth')
          $auth = Configure::read('Security.auth');
          if (!$auth) {
              return;
          }
          if (!is_array($auth)) {
              throw new Exception("`Security.auth` config value must be array.");
          }
          $this->Auth->authenticate = array_merge($auth, $this->Auth->authenticate);
          // Disable Form authentication
          if (Configure::read('Security.auth_enforced')) {
              unset($this->Auth->authenticate['Form']);
          }
          if ($this->Auth->startup($this)) {
              $user = $this->Auth->user();
              if ($user) {
                  $this->User->updateLoginTimes($user);
                  // User found in the db, add the user info to the session
                  $this->Session->renew();
                  $this->Session->write(AuthComponent::$sessionKey, $user);
              }
          }
      }
  }
  ```

test "rank1394: the same plugin login refuses to establish the session while an OTP challenge is outstanding"
  lang php
  file app/Controller/AppController.php
  reject VYQL-AUTH-004
  reject_review code.AuthFlowBypassReview
  reject_review code.MissingSessionRotationAfterAuthentication
  code
  ```
  <?php
  App::uses('Controller', 'Controller');

  class AppController extends Controller
  {
      public function beforeFilter()
      {
          if (!$this->Session->read(AuthComponent::$sessionKey)) {
              $this->_loadAuthenticationPlugins();
          }
      }

      /**
       * @throws Exception
       */
      protected function _loadAuthenticationPlugins()
      {
          // load authentication plugins from Configure::read('Security.auth')
          $auth = Configure::read('Security.auth');
          if (!$auth) {
              return;
          }
          if (!is_array($auth)) {
              throw new Exception("`Security.auth` config value must be array.");
          }
          $this->Auth->authenticate = array_merge($auth, $this->Auth->authenticate);
          // Disable Form authentication
          if (Configure::read('Security.auth_enforced')) {
              unset($this->Auth->authenticate['Form']);
          }
          if ($this->Auth->startup($this)) {
              $user = $this->Auth->user();
              if ($user) {
                  // A user authenticated by an authentication plugin (e.g. LDAP) gets
                  // logged in here, during beforeFilter, before UsersController::login()
                  // runs. If the user has OTP enabled we must enforce the OTP challenge at
                  // this point too.
                  if ($this->__pluginLoginRequiresOtp($user)) {
                      return;
                  }
                  $this->User->updateLoginTimes($user);
                  // User found in the db, add the user info to the session
                  $this->Session->renew();
                  $this->Session->write(AuthComponent::$sessionKey, $user);
              }
          }
      }

      /**
       * @param array $user The user record returned by the authentication plugin
       * @return bool True if the user still needs to pass an OTP challenge.
       */
      private function __pluginLoginRequiresOtp(array $user)
      {
          if (!empty($user['disabled'])) {
              return false;
          }

          $otpAction = null;
          // TOTP / HOTP
          if (
              !Configure::read('Security.otp_disabled') &&
              !empty($user['totp']) &&
              class_exists('\OTPHP\TOTP')
          ) {
              $this->Session->write('otp_user', $user);
              $otpAction = 'otp';
          // E-mail OTP
          } elseif (Configure::read('Security.email_otp_enabled')) {
              $this->Session->write('email_otp_user', $user);
              $otpAction = 'email_otp';
          }

          if ($otpAction === null) {
              return false;
          }

          $currentAction = isset($this->request->params['action']) ?
              $this->request->params['action'] : null;
          if (!in_array($currentAction, ['otp', 'email_otp'], true)) {
              $this->redirect(['controller' => 'users', 'action' => $otpAction]);
          }
          return true;
      }
  }
  ```

test "rank1394: the same guard under a helper name carrying no second-factor vocabulary"
  lang php
  file app/Controller/AppController.php
  reject VYQL-AUTH-004
  reject_review code.AuthFlowBypassReview
  reject_review code.MissingSessionRotationAfterAuthentication
  code
  ```
  <?php
  App::uses('Controller', 'Controller');

  class AppController extends Controller
  {
      protected function _loadAuthenticationPlugins()
      {
          $auth = Configure::read('Security.auth');
          if (!$auth) {
              return;
          }
          $this->Auth->authenticate = array_merge($auth, $this->Auth->authenticate);
          if (Configure::read('Security.auth_enforced')) {
              unset($this->Auth->authenticate['Form']);
          }
          if ($this->Auth->startup($this)) {
              $user = $this->Auth->user();
              if ($user) {
                  if ($this->__pluginLoginRequiresSecondFactor($user)) {
                      return;
                  }
                  $this->User->updateLoginTimes($user);
                  $this->Session->renew();
                  $this->Session->write(AuthComponent::$sessionKey, $user);
              }
          }
      }

      private function __pluginLoginRequiresSecondFactor(array $user)
      {
          if (!empty($user['disabled'])) {
              return false;
          }

          $challenge = null;
          if (
              !Configure::read('Security.otp_disabled') &&
              !empty($user['totp']) &&
              class_exists('\OTPHP\TOTP')
          ) {
              $this->Session->write('otp_user', $user);
              $challenge = 'otp';
          } elseif (Configure::read('Security.email_otp_enabled')) {
              $this->Session->write('email_otp_user', $user);
              $challenge = 'email_otp';
          }

          if ($challenge === null) {
              return false;
          }

          $currentAction = isset($this->request->params['action']) ?
              $this->request->params['action'] : null;
          if (!in_array($currentAction, ['otp', 'email_otp'], true)) {
              $this->redirect(['controller' => 'users', 'action' => $challenge]);
          }
          return true;
      }
  }
  ```

test "rank1394: an API key authentication path establishes the same session key and needs no second factor"
  lang php
  file app/Controller/AppController.php
  reject VYQL-AUTH-004
  reject_review code.AuthFlowBypassReview
  reject_review code.MissingSessionRotationAfterAuthentication
  code
  ```
  <?php
  App::uses('Controller', 'Controller');

  class AppController extends Controller
  {
      private function __loginByAuthKey()
      {
          $authKey = $this->_readHttpAuthorizationHeader();
          if (empty($authKey)) {
              return false;
          }
          $user = $this->checkAuthUser($authKey);
          if ($user) {
              $start = substr($authKey, 0, 4);
              $end = substr($authKey, -4);
              $this->__logApiKeyUse($start . $end);
              $this->User->updateAPIAccessTime($user);
              $this->Session->renew();
              $this->Session->write(AuthComponent::$sessionKey, $user);
              $this->isApiAuthed = true;
              return true;
          }
          // User not authenticated correctly: reset the session information
          $this->Session->destroy();
          return false;
      }
  }
  ```
